<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>{{ title }}</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --serif: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia, serif;
      --sans: "IBM Plex Sans", "Source Sans 3", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      --mono: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    }
    html[data-theme="dark"] {
      --bg: #12110f;
      --bg-2: #1c1a17;
      --ink: #ece6dc;
      --muted: #a39a8c;
      --line: #2e2a25;
      --accent: #e07a5f;
      --accent-2: #81b0c7;
      --accent-3: #c3a572;
      --good: #8fb89a;
      --bad: #d67b7b;
      --banner: #3a2a1c;
    }
    html[data-theme="light"] {
      --bg: #f3efe6;
      --bg-2: #fffaf1;
      --ink: #1a1714;
      --muted: #6b645c;
      --line: #ddd4c6;
      --accent: #9c2f2f;
      --accent-2: #2c4a6e;
      --accent-3: #8a5a12;
      --good: #2f5d3a;
      --bad: #8f2d2d;
      --banner: #f3e0c8;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); }
    body {
      font-family: var(--sans);
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      max-width: 1080px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 32px 24px 80px;
    }
    header.mast {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: baseline;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding-bottom: 16px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
      gap: 16px;
    }
    .brand {
      font-family: var(--serif);
      font-size: 13px;
      letter-spacing: 0.16em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    h1 {
      font-family: var(--serif);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 32px;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      margin: 4px 0 0;
    }
    .sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
    button.theme {
      background: var(--bg-2);
      color: var(--ink);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 6px 10px;
      font-family: var(--sans);
      font-size: 12px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .banner {
      background: var(--banner);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 12px 16px;
      margin: 0 0 24px;
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .banner strong { color: var(--accent); }
    .hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px, 1fr));
      gap: 12px;
      margin: 0 0 28px;
    }
    .tile {
      background: var(--bg-2);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 14px 16px;
    }
    .tile .k {
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .tile .v {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 26px;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      margin-top: 4px;
    }
    .tile .u { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
    h2 {
      font-family: var(--serif);
      font-size: 22px;
      margin: 36px 0 12px;
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    h3 { font-size: 15px; margin: 20px 0 8px; }
    .grid-2 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 12px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 720px) { .grid-2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    dl.kv {
      background: var(--bg-2);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 12px 16px;
      margin: 0;
    }
    dl.kv div { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; padding: 3px 0; }
    dl.kv dt { color: var(--muted); }
    dl.kv dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; text-align: right; }
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    th, td {
      text-align: left;
      padding: 8px 10px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    th { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-family: var(--mono); }
    .ok { color: var(--good); }
    .bad { color: var(--bad); }
    .warn { color: var(--accent-3); }
    .chart { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 8px 0 20px; }
    .chart-title { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 14px; }
    .chart-unit { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 10px; font-family: var(--sans); }
    .grid { stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
    .tick { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 10px; font-family: var(--mono); }
    .legend { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; font-family: var(--sans); }
    .bar-0 { fill: var(--accent); }
    .bar-1 { fill: var(--accent-2); }
    .bar-2 { fill: var(--accent-3); }
    footer {
      margin-top: 48px;
      padding-top: 16px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    ul.notes { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; padding-left: 18px; }
    details { margin: 8px 0; }
    summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="mast">
    <div>
      <div class="brand">local-llm-bench · v{{ version }}</div>
      <h1>{{ heading }}</h1>
      <div class="sub">{{ subtitle }}</div>
    </div>
    <button class="theme" type="button" id="theme-btn">Light</button>
  </header>

  {% if synthetic %}
  <div class="banner" role="status">
    <strong>Synthetic data.</strong>
    These numbers were produced by the in-process mock backend, not by a real model on this machine.
    Do not cite them as hardware performance.
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if warnings %}
  <div class="banner" role="status">
    <strong>Warnings.</strong>
    <ul class="notes">{% for w in warnings %}<li>{{ w }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <section class="hero">
    {% for tile in tiles %}
    <div class="tile">
      <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}</div>
      <div class="v">{{ tile.value }} <span class="u">{{ tile.unit }}</span></div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>

  {{ hardware_html | safe }}
  {{ quality_html | safe }}
  {{ charts_html | safe }}
  {{ tables_html | safe }}

  <h2>How to read this</h2>
  <ul class="notes">
    <li>TTFT is client-observed time to first <em>content</em> token. It includes queueing, prefill, and the first decode step.</li>
    <li>Decode tok/s excludes that first token: (output tokens − 1) / (last token − first token).</li>
    <li>Prefill (server) is uncached prompt tokens / uncached prompt ms. The proxy column is prompt_tokens/TTFT and is never mixed into server prefill.</li>
    <li>p50 / p95 are linear-interpolation percentiles over successful measured trials (warmup discarded).</li>
    <li>Harness overhead is the client floor measured against a zero-delay mock. Subtract it from TTFT for a lower bound on server time.</li>
    <li>VRAM is device-level when NVML/nvidia-smi is available, sampled on a niced background thread (~4 Hz, 1 Hz for nvidia-smi).</li>
  </ul>

  <footer>
    Generated by local-llm-bench {{ version }} · schema {{ schema_version }} ·
    self-contained file (no network). Theme preference stored in localStorage.
  </footer>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.documentElement;
      var btn = document.getElementById("theme-btn");
      var stored = localStorage.getItem("llmbench-theme");
      function apply(theme) {
        root.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
        btn.textContent = theme === "dark" ? "Light" : "Dark";
      }
      apply(stored === "light" ? "light" : "dark");
      btn.addEventListener("click", function () {
        var next = root.getAttribute("data-theme") === "dark" ? "light" : "dark";
        localStorage.setItem("llmbench-theme", next);
        apply(next);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
